        "brief": "Create a Java exercise for first-year students about applying small business rules to a list of library checkout events. Students should compute useful summaries such as overdue counts, total fees, and member-specific activity. Keep the domain realistic and compact. Include representative edge cases such as empty input, duplicate members, and invalid durations. Do not assume any particular class or method names from me.\n",
